      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. You're basically saying their logic is completely disconnected from how the economy actually functions. \n\nIf my student wants to win on the \"fairness\" or \"moral\" front of the debate, how should they handle the argument that UBI is actually more 'fair' because it removes the stigma and bureaucracy of current welfare? They'll probably argue that the current system is punitive and treats people like they're untrustworthy. How can the opposition counter that moral high ground without just sounding like they're against helping people?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
